 ## Background
-The algorithm was introduced by Matt Pharr in 1996, often referred to as "Hart's Sphere Tracing" after Jim Blinn's earlier work on sphere tracing, but formalized with the Lipschitz bound guarantee by Pharr [S3]. It belongs to the ray-marching family and is widely used in real-time rendering, including games and shaders, due to its simplicity and robustness [S3]. Extensions such as Segment Tracing have been proposed to address its limitations by using local Lipschitz bounds [S1, S3].
